{"title":"Career Roadmap · Agri-Tech Engineer","role":"Agri-Tech Engineer","summary":"An Agri-Tech Engineer applies engineering, electronics, IoT, automation, data science, AI and agricultural knowledge to improve farm productivity, resource efficiency, crop monitoring, mechanisation and agricultural decision-making.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The role can cover:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Precision agriculture"},{"text":"Smart irrigation"},{"text":"Agricultural robotics"},{"text":"Farm automation"},{"text":"Drones and remote sensing"},{"text":"IoT-based farming"},{"text":"Soil and crop monitoring"},{"text":"AI-based crop analysis"},{"text":"Agricultural machinery"},{"text":"Post-harvest technology"},{"text":"Controlled-environment agriculture"},{"text":"Digital agriculture platforms"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Agricultural Engineering is a strong direct pathway, particularly for hardware, mechanisation, irrigation, farm automation and agricultural systems. Students should add IoT, GIS, remote sensing, Python, AI/ML and embedded systems to become competitive for modern Agri-Tech roles."},{"type":"note","label":"Career positioning","text":"Agri-Tech Engineer can be an entry-level role, but \"Agri-Tech Engineer\" is a broad industry title. Depending on the employer, the actual job may be called Precision Agriculture Engineer, Agricultural Automation Engineer, IoT Engineer, Farm Technology Engineer, GIS/Remote-Sensing Engineer or Agricultural Robotics Engineer."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech + Agri-Tech projects/internships"},{"text":"Agricultural engineering + IoT + data"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Junior Agri-Tech / Precision Agriculture Engineer"},{"text":"Sensors, farm systems, automation"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text"